INV-fibis's RECALL half, and the next link after INV-jujoh (#480) made these
calls emit at all. `class_field_types` is dict[str, dict[str, Symbol]] --
Symbol-valued, so BY CONSTRUCTION it can only ever hold an in-repo class.
Locals have had both halves since WI-fuvuj (`var_types` /
`external_var_types`); fields had only the first:

    s = socket.socket();          s.sendall(x)        -> socket.socket   SEEN
    self.sock = socket.socket();  self.sock.sendall(x) -> external       BLIND

Two spellings of one fact, one of them visible. `class_external_field_types`
is the missing counterpart, populated from the three shapes an __init__ can
establish a field type from -- annotated parameter, external constructor,
annotated field declaration -- each reusing that shape's EXISTING resolver so
the INV-kipor binding check is inherited rather than re-decided.

