NAMESPACED `self.<field>`, unlike the in-repo merge which uses the bare field
name. `external_var_types` is MUTATED as the body is walked, so a bare-keyed
field type would be silently overwritten by a same-named local assigned later
and would thereafter answer for the field. Namespacing makes that collision
structurally impossible rather than relying on an ordering that holds today.

